From ddb8d64e4095740b8acb490760754936d81010ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 04:44:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] LinearSolverFactory: Chebyshev smoother of MFEM as
 preconditioner

OperatorChebyshevSmoother (options Order, 2 by default, and
NumberOfPowerIterations, 10 by default): Chebyshev smoother of MFEM, whose
diagonal is computed as for the Jacobi smoother (AssembleDiagonal, or
GetDiag for a sparse matrix) and whose largest eigenvalue is estimated by
the power method, on all the processes, each time the operator changes.
It only uses products by the operator and its diagonal: usable with the
tangent operator applied without assembly.

Tests: OperatorSmoothersTest (Laplace equation on a square, sequential and
2 processes: the conjugate gradient makes 46 iterations with the Jacobi
smoother, 27 and 17 with the Chebyshev smoothers of order 2 and 4, the
same numbers for the assembled operator and for an operator applied
without assembly; mutations of the order and of the communicator
detected), and a case of BatchIntegrationTest with the tangent operator
applied without assembly preconditioned by the Chebyshev smoother.
Glossary: Jacobi and Chebyshev smoothers.
